# Cursor Rules for Agentix (agx) Workspace

You are assisting in a project using **Agentix (agx)** multi-agent orchestration.

## 1. Operating Environment & Worktrees
This repository uses isolated Git worktrees to separate backend, frontend, and lead integration work:
- Backend files (`app/`, `database/`, `routes/`, `tests/`) belong exclusively to `agent/backend` in `../<project>-backend`.
- Frontend files (`resources/views/`, `public/assets/`, UI components) belong exclusively to `agent/frontend` in `../<project>-frontend`.
- Design documentation, tokens, and visual QA belong to root (`main`).

## 2. CLI Usage (`agx`)
Instead of manual git worktree manipulation, instruct or execute via `agx`:
- `agx st`: Check team and worktree status.
- `agx sync`: Sync worktrees with `main`.
- `agx run -b "<backend>" -f "<frontend>"`: Concurrent worker dispatch.
- `agx diff`: Review PR diffs.
- `agx t -f <filter>`: Run automated tests.
- `agx vqa -u <url>`: Playwright multi-viewport browser capture (Mobile 375px, Tablet 768px, Desktop 1440px).
- `agx merge -f <filter>`: Integrate reviewed branches into `main`.
- `agx p -m "<msg>"`: Commit and push.

## 3. UI/UX Refactoring Standards
Whenever writing frontend code or reviewing interfaces:
- Enforce the 7 Master UI Recipes (`ui-refactor.md`):
  1. Sharpen Message: Exactly ONE focal accent span.
  2. Break Symmetry: 60/40 or 65/35 asymmetric grid with floating anchor badge.
  3. Build Argument: Coherent section rhythm with kickers and hairline dividers.
  4. Pick Winner: Elevate flagship tier (60% weight) over uniform cards.
  5. Scale Type: 4-tier scale (Display, Title, Body, Kicker).
  6. Give Color Meaning: Disciplined semantic palette (60-30-10 rule).
  7. Add Signature: Section kickers with pulsing status dots.
- Anti-AI-Slop: Ban purple-cyan gradients, floating glass cards, sparkle emojis, and uniform bento grids.
- UI-Mandatory: Zero dead buttons or fake `#` links; mobile responsive down to 375px without horizontal scroll.
